    "body": "Reopened. The work on this issue is not finished.\n\nGitHub closed #1616 when PR #1632 merged (2026-11-14, 10:06 UTC). Commit `a1833e52` on that branch carries `Fixes #1616` in its message. The PR body said `Refs #1616`, and the branch's own decision file says the PR does not close the issue: `docs/decisions/1616-first-traverse-clearance.md`.\n\nState of \"Done means\" now:\n- grblHAL and TinyG, and Carvera at program start: done in PR #1632.\n- Fanuc family posts (fanuc, haas, mazak, doosan-dnm, sinumerik, heidenhain): done in PR #1636, tracked by #1633 (closed).\n- Carvera right after `M6`: not done. PR #1632 kept main's order there: a bare `G0 X.. Y..` first, at the changer's exit height, then the clearance Z line. The decision file records this as an open hazard: nothing read so far confirms the exit height clears the part with a long tool.\n\nRemaining scope: state the clearance height before the first X/Y traverse after `M6` on Carvera, or record and pin a proven-safe order. #1616 is `P1` on the v0.20.0 cut list. The cut start check now sees it open again.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
